			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates completing terminal race fix\n\nSynchronize Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Mountain (c2d0beca): Complete the terminal race-condition fix by deferring the `sky://terminal/create` event with a 120ms delay. This addresses the timing vulnerability where the Tauri event arrived before `_ptys.set(id, pty)` completed during step 1 (RPC in-flight), causing `_ptys.get(id)` to return undefined and silently dropping keystrokes. Complements the earlier fix in c99ccbe that added the `AppendTerminalOutput` replay buffer for data events.\n- Output (8d7a19d): Add disabled `PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration` transform that defaults `terminal.integrated.gpuAcceleration` to `'off'` to work around xterm.js WebGL texture atlas font drift in WKWebView. Available on-disk for re-enabling if needed.\n- Cocoon (4336123): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nThis synchronization completes the terminal race-condition fix cycle that began with bf94e30, restoring proper terminal panel functionality.",
			"SHA": "8e808838d772556db83ca0d4bd0d22c2dde6ada1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:20:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Return integer id from localPty:createProcess\n\nSynchronize Mountain to c99ccbe7 which fixes the blank terminal panels issue. The VS Code terminal workbench expects `IPtyService.createProcess` to return a `Promise<number>` (the integer terminal id), but Mountain was returning the full `{id, name, pid}` object. This caused the workbench to key its internal `_ptys` map incorrectly, making `_ptys.get(<integer>)` lookups return `undefined` from `onProcessData`/`onProcessReady`, resulting in xterm receiving zero bytes despite Mountain's PTY reader emitting data continuously.\n\nThe fix splits the terminal handler into three distinct paths: spawn preserves full response for Cocoon's Sky bridge, createProcess returns only the integer id per VS Code contract, and start is a no-op for the eager-spawn pattern.\n\nAlso sync Cocoon submodule to 15690303.",
			"SHA": "bf94e30b447208b59dc62d5ad0d591a239a6a530"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:00:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates across Element fleet\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Mountain (db5f0f7): Rename binary/library targets to \"Mountain\", simplify tauri.conf.json identifiers and remove duplicate externalBin entry.\n- Sky (d574527): Fix 0-based line indexing bug in search results RangeLocations causing 'undefined' errors, add Mountain.dev.log diagnostic bridging for service shape probing.\n- Maintain (0d1cee9): Rebuild CHANGELOG with quarter-based versioning, add v1.3 and v1.0 sections missing from release history.\n- Worker (0e2d546): Expand CHANGELOG from 61 to 134 lines documenting complete version history v2.1→v0.0 with commit refs.\n- Echo (1f3c848): Bump miniflare and wrangler dev dependencies.\n- Cocoon (01322bf): Submodule sync to latest.\n\nBrings cross-cutting synchronizations including search functionality fix and documentation improvements across the Element umbrella.",
			"SHA": "220904a60b893a9bb5283c60706891711a20add7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T15:59:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				8
			],
			"Message": "docs(Element): Rewrite umbrella CHANGELOG with Keep a Changelog format\n\nRestructure Land/Element/CHANGELOG.md from a placeholder entry to a comprehensive narrative tracking cross-cutting submodule synchronizations. The rewrite adds: an intro explaining Element as the fleet umbrella whose submodules are the actual elements; v2.2 documenting the bundled-electron correctness pass sync of Output and Sky; v2.1 documenting the Full Workbench Lift CHANGELOG rewrite cycle across Common, Air, Wind, Cocoon; and v0.0 for project inception.\n\nSubmodule updates: Echo (CHANGELOG rebuild with full history), Grove (Keep a Changelog format), Mist (commit references and dates), Rest (Keep-a-Changelog overhaul), SideCar (narrative release history), Vine (restructured for clarity).\n\nAligns the Element umbrella documentation with the prose-style CHANGELOG format established across other Land components.",
			"SHA": "2d6e601af107838cc9fcac3b3fe20794cf42a41c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T05:27:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Revise CHANGELOG with narrative formatting\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing Common to fd25cb49. The CHANGELOG has been restructured to use a more readable, narrative-driven format inspired by Keep a Changelog. Changes include: adding an introductory paragraph explaining Common's purpose as the abstract core with trait definitions and DTOs; rewriting version headers from [Common/vX.X] to [vX.X] for consistency; converting bullet-point changes to flowing prose descriptions; and aligning all version entries with consistent voice and structure.\n\nThis revision improves scannability and aligns Common's documentation with the prose-style CHANGELOG format established across other Land components, while preserving all historical change information.",
			"SHA": "215fc0b17612e5e2a194e8c49463984fe48e28d0"
